{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"With a non-default configured port and no origin record, the CLI can send the daemon token to a different service on port 7400."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"compat","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After rollback rotates the token without updating the origin record, newer clients omit authentication and protected requests fail until the stale record is removed or replaced."}]}